A||||8||Jncomutt||Engine Bang, Dog Bone??||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||08-07-2001||02:09 PM||||When ever I start off from a complete stop, the engine shakes and sort of 'bangs' as I start to let off the clutch until I get going, then its fine.  I was told this could be the dog bone.  It appears that the rubber bushings now have an oval opening in them as if they've been stretched, so I'm thinking this is it.  <P>My question is, am I better off purchasing the "ultimate dog bone"  or just replacing the bushings?  Is there any advantages of this over the stock piece??<P><BR>EDIT:  Its an 84, so its got the 4cyl.<BR>  (not sure if that matters)<p>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bluebottlejunky||08-07-2001||02:19 PM||||I would say bushings..i had the same proublem with my 85 gt..I got new poly bushings for my dog bone...and it stoped shakin..runs great now! fierostore.com I think has them..<P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jncomutt||08-07-2001||02:29 PM||||Guess I'll try just the bushings.  Can I just unbolt one side, change the bushings, put it back, then disconnect the other side, change, and reconnect??  Or does it have to be held in place??  (sorry for the fact I'm a moron)||||reg||1
Z||000003||starfighter007@msn.com||08-07-2001||02:42 PM||||Well I dont think you are a moron. But when you take the dog bone out to change the bushings you may as well take it cmpletely out as this will be easier for you to do and it wont make a difference , just a little harder to change the bushings while the bone is in the car&gt;how ever while its out be careful where you set so no stray dogs see it and take it||||reg||6
Z||000004||1FST2M6||08-07-2001||03:14 PM||||i'm sure the dog bone is toast.. but if it bangs as you say it does i'd but my $ on failing/failed exhaust hangers... the exhaust moves WAY more than the engine itself and having messed with a few i've noticed that the engines can't hit anything unless the dog bone is completly broken in 2.. and even then the front engine mounts will keep it about 1" from the fire wall..  so check your exhaust first.. then get a dog bone. Ultimate only don't waste your time and $ on another stock one.  nicer dog bones available at <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrantsig.jpg">           <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||08-07-2001||03:18 PM||||I would also check the 2 trans mounts and the front engine mount on the bottom. If the dog bone is "ovaled" then the other mounts are most likely worn too. Haze and I changed his mounts and it was a world of improvement.<BR>All the original mounts were "soft" compared to the new mounts.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jncomutt||08-07-2001||06:07 PM||||Hey, Come to find out, the exhaust had 3 springs that were not connected.  I reconnected them, but the noise is still there.  It did have an effect, its not as noisy now.  I'm going to go ahead and order the ultimate from The Fiero Store and see what happens there.<P>Also, i just realized that since this started happening, my clutch has started slipping.  Could these two be related???||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||08-07-2001||07:23 PM||||If the 4 cyl dogbone is worn, it can cause the air filter to smack the trunk wall when you accelerate. Sure did, with mine. Bad for the throttle body and such. Ogre's Cave (link at bottom of page) talks about engine mounts, dog bones, and a lot of other interesting stuff. <BR>Don't think the slipping clutch is related. But if it's chattering, you're gonna beat hell out of your trunk and air filter.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jncomutt||08-08-2001||02:37 PM||||Well, I just got back from The Fiero Store.  I picked up an ultimate dog bone.  Had a lil trouble with getting the bolt thru closest to the trunk, but with 2 hands, and my friend pushin the bolt, we made it happen.<P>And Wow, what a difference.  The car accelerates Much smoother, the 'bang' is gone, so is that lil' rattle and shutter (I think was the exhaust)   Once again, you guys are awesome...||||reg||1
